# Photosynthetic photon flux density at the canopy, 400-700 nm. Minted because
# the standard set carries no photon-flux type (ADR-0005 d2).
#
# mol per square metre per second, unscaled SI. The horticultural convention is
# micromol, and micro is a display prefix -- the same argument ADR-0005 rev 1
# made for joule over watt-hour. 300 umol/m2/s is 300e-6 here.
#
# Reconstructed on the node from the ten in-window band counts by the
# coefficients of M02 spec 6.2, which are a COMMISSIONING property of one
# luminaire spectrum and one optical stack, not a device constant. Until they
# are written to the node they do not exist, and `valid` is what says so: an
# uncommissioned node publishes this subject with valid = false rather than
# falling silent, so that a gateway can tell an uncommissioned module from an
# absent one.
#
# DLI -- this quantity integrated over the photoperiod -- is the gateway's
# (M02 spec 3.2, ADR-0014 d4). It is not derived here and has no field here.
uavcan.time.SynchronizedTimestamp.1.0 timestamp
float32 mol_per_square_metre_per_second
bool valid   # true = a reconstruction coefficient set is loaded and the bands read
@extent 16 * 8
